//
// QWEN2.5-3B BF16 prefill TTFT vs padded prefill length, into
// qwen25_3b.prefill_sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
//
// The other axis from run_npu2_sweep.lit: that one walks KV depth for decode
// tok/s, this one walks the length the prefill ELFs are BUILT for. TTFT tracks
// the built length, not the prompt -- these prefills pad the prompt to it and
// read the last real token's row -- so every point here rebuilds the engines,
// into a per-CTX cache directory. KernelCache keys entries on kernel name
// alone, so one directory shared across lengths would silently time the
// previous length's ELFs; sweep_prefill.py independently guards that by reading
// the built length off the "prefill kernels (seq_len=N)" line.
//
// Latency only, never a correctness gate (run_npu2_verify.lit is that).
//
// 512 and 1024 are swept but expected to fail, with the status naming why:
// stitcher_mixed_tile_m. Every shape this model needs is in the registry at
// those lengths and every row is measured -- but the registry's best method
// FLIPS with length: the square Q/O proj is fused-cast (tile_m=64) at M=2048
// and drain (tile_m=32) at 512/1024. This model's prefill stitcher fuses
// several GEMMs into one ELF and assumes they share a tile_m, which held while
// M=2048 was the only reachable length. Closing it is a stitcher change, not a
// registry one.
//
// Measured on a Ryzen AI 9 HX 370:
//   2048 -> 4649 ms
//   4096 -> 10338 ms
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, hf_token, hfweights_qwen_qwen2_5_3b_instruct
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name qwen25_3b --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,1024,2048,4096 --expect-fail 512,1024 --seq-env LLM_SEQ_LEN --bench-env LLM_BENCH_L --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out qwen25_3b.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < qwen25_3b.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "qwen25_3b"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// A parsed number at the reference length, not just a well-formed file: if the
// driver's TTFT line drifts out of sweep_prefill.py's regex every point goes
// null and the published curve silently empties while the test stays green.
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
